  "conclusion": "The rejected field service_ready_known is absent from actual observe_protocol trays. It belongs to planning capture rows. All three saved A decisions had an already-validated own loading-to-loaded transition and an earliest source-service completion bound1.1. The .11+.01 strict wire guard can be checked against that derived bound without adding fields to or changing the native view. No actual route was submitted in this experiment.",
  "native_source_chain": {
    "binding_lines": "circulation_session_binding.hpp:190-226 excludes service_ready fields from observe tray;707-708 adds them to planning capture serialization.",
    "load_to_leg": "circulation_runtime_impl.hpp:723-728 records LOAD_COMPLETE, sets loaded_at and creates the active leg;227-273 releases that leg no earlier than the completion time.",
    "earliest_service": "event_driven_junction.hpp:6454,6479-6480,6576,6610 uses source service duration, reservations at admission time+duration, and scheduled finish. Admission waiting can delay this bound, not make it earlier.",
    "route_validation": "circulation_runtime_impl.hpp:490-544 checks current generation/public traversal/from/uncommitted active leg, owner/business/permission/directed edge/static suffix/deadline/can_enter. Updated is a preference, not a reserved future edge."
  },
  "test_gap": "The frozen synthetic A stub included service_ready_known/service_ready_at in a supposed observe_protocol tray, so it missed this actual endpoint schema error. Keep those passed results in their synthetic scope; new regressions must use these exact real endpoint rows and missing fields.",
